                <pb facs="0583" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3039: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ramer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-18T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                                1924—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Your March 17, 4 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d414-f1"/> You may inquire of the
                    Nicaraguan Government whether it would have any objection to the detail of four
                        <pb facs="0584" n="490" xml:id="pg490"/> Marines in civilian clothes to
                    assist Dodds at Chinandega next Sunday, pointing out that the Nicaraguan
                    Government’s note of December 13 last<anchor n="6" xml:id="d414-f2"/> indicated
                    that it would approve of the appointment of members of the Marine detachment as
                    assistants to Dodds, should that prove necessary. If the Nicaraguan Government
                    has no objection to this arrangement, you may ask the Commander of the Legation
                    guard to detail four men of tact and discretion, with a good knowledge of
                    Spanish, to work under Dodds’ direction on Sunday next.</p>
                <p>The Department assumes from your transmission of Dodds’ request without comment
                    that you approve of the same.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
